From 9a850c4e7fcfc32c78a89a3771ae31ed6fc214d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Roberts-Baca <jacobrobertsbaca@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:30:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Host rustc on WASI, for the debugger.sh engine.

Lets rustc be built for, and run on, wasm32-wasip1, which has no threads and
no dynamic libraries. It compiles crates to objects, which are linked
separately. Building on bjorn3's work to host rustc on WebAssembly.

- Run the compiler on the main thread, whose stack size is set when rustc is
  linked, and the jobserver proxy without a helper thread.
- Codegen without threads: the coordinator runs once codegen is done, and its
  work items as it spawns them. The threads only ever communicate through
  channels, so this replays the messages of a run in which each codegen unit
  finishes instantly. Also write the allocator shim as an object, since it
  can't be linked in.
- Report that dynamic libraries (codegen backends, proc macros, Enzyme and
  offloading) can't be loaded, and default to the root as the sysroot.
- Exit on fatal errors rather than unwinding (rustc is built with
  panic=abort), don't check that LLVM supports threads or that outputs are
  writable (WASI has no permissions), and use no process ID.
- Build rustc_driver as an rlib too, and link LLVM against libc++.
- Bootstrap: let rustc_llvm describe a WASI host's LLVM with its configured
  llvm-config, which runs on the build machine.
